   "plaque": "dyo_llynfell",
   "title": "The River Llynfell",
   "text": "The River Llynfell sinks into the hill here and works its way out below. A river and its cave are the same thing seen at different times: the water cuts, the passage stays, and the next river moves in on top."
  },
  {
   "x": 7,
   "y": 2,
   "plaque": "dyo_morgan_brothers",
   "title": "The Morgan Brothers",
   "text": "In 1912 the brothers Tommy and Jeff Morgan, from Abercrave, followed the river into the hill in a coracle with only candles for light. They found the cave that is now a show cave. Nobody had thought to take a torch, and nobody wrote down whose idea the coracle was."
  }
